+# Build menu: kept panel and pages
+
+## The problem
+
+Each tab page was built inside a Vide `switch`, so every tab switch destroyed the old page and
+built the new one. Building Shapes created about 450 instances (40 ms frame against an 8 ms idle)
+and Colors about 370 (30 ms). The panel itself sat in a `show` in `Main.client.luau`, so every
+close destroyed it and every open rebuilt the panel plus the current page.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **The panel is built on the first open and then kept.** `Main.client.luau` mounts it once
+  `isMenuOpen` has been true once, and passes `isMenuOpen` as `Present`. Closing slides it out
+  as before. Once it is fully below the screen it is hidden with `Visible = false`, not
+  destroyed.
+- **Each tab page is built on its first visit and then kept.** `BuildMenu.luau` replaces
+  `switch` with `indexes` over a map of every tab visited so far, so no page is ever destroyed.
+  Pages not on show are hidden with `Visible = false`.
+- **The look and animation are unchanged:**
+  - The panel's own "built" flag starts false, so the first open still slides in from below.
+    Every later open slides in from the resting position below the screen, as a rebuilt panel
+    did. Reopening during the slide-out reverses the slide, which is also what the old `show`
+    did.
+  - A kept Shapes or Colors page scrolls back to the top each time it comes on screen, as a
+    rebuilt page started.
+  - The rainbow swatch's hue restarts at 0 each time it comes on screen, as a rebuilt swatch
+    did.
+- **No work while hidden.** The rainbow swatch's `Heartbeat` connection now runs only while the
+  Colors page is on show and the panel is open or still sliding out. Before, a kept page would
+  have kept it running forever.
+
+Cost: the first visit to each tab, and the first open, still build the same instances, so they
+still stall once per play session. After that, Blocks, Colors, and Shapes (about 900 instances in
+total) stay in memory while hidden.
+
+## How to check it in Studio
+
+1. Start a playtest (F5) and open the MicroProfiler (Ctrl+F6). Pause it with Ctrl+P when you want
+   to read a frame.
+2. Open the menu with M, then switch Blocks, Colors, Shapes once each. These first visits should
+   still show the 30 to 40 ms frames: that is the one-time build.
+3. Now switch between the tabs several more times, and close and reopen the menu on Shapes and on
+   Colors. The frame of each switch or open should stay near the idle 8 ms, with no spike.
+4. To confirm nothing is being built, run this in the command bar during the playtest (client
+   side), then switch tabs and open and close the menu a few times:
+
+   ```lua
+   local gui = game.Players.LocalPlayer.PlayerGui:WaitForChild("BuildMenuGui")
+   local added = 0
+   gui.DescendantAdded:Connect(function() added += 1 end)
+   task.delay(10, function() print("instances added in 10 s:", added) end)
+   ```
+
+   After every tab has been visited once, it should print 0. Before this change, each switch to
+   Shapes added about 450.
+5. Check the look: the first open still slides up, closing slides down, later opens slide up
+   again, the rainbow swatch cycles on Colors, and a scrolled Shapes page is back at the top
+   when you return to it.
